  "scenario": "A 2,000 L mammalian-cell bioreactor producing a secreted therapeutic protein has seen product titer fall about 30% over the last three weeks, and the loss has persisted across several batches. The decline began shortly after a maintenance shutdown in which a feed-water line fitting was replaced and probes were recalibrated. The operators' leading theories are dissolved-oxygen control drift or a temperature excursion. Batch records note the broth has looked cloudier than usual at harvest. Routine panels look broadly within range. The feed-water system, gas train, cooling jacket, and dosing pumps are all instrumented and adjustable. You have a limited number of experiments; you may measure quantities and apply available controls or additives, alone or in combination. Determine what is really driving the loss and what to do about it.",
